8. 🛑 WHY SECTION 6 IS NOT COMPUTABLE, AND WHAT THAT ITSELF SHOWS
====================================================================================================================
  A burst-conditioned band RMS needs 4 s windows lying wholly inside (or wholly outside)
  a burst.  At < 16 km/h:
     STOCK burst duty 0.056, LONGEST BURST 0.69 s  =>  ZERO windows fit inside a burst,
       at 4 s, at 2 s, or even at 1 s.  ⇒ STOCK'S MODE NEVER SUSTAINS FOR ONE SECOND.
     6x builds duty 0.93-0.95            =>  ZERO windows fit wholly OUTSIDE a burst.
  ⇒ THE TWO ARMS HAVE NO OVERLAPPING CONDITION.  The contrast cannot be conditioned.

  ⭐ AND THE DIRECTION OF THE POOLING ARTIFACT IS THE OPPOSITE OF WHAT WAS FEARED:
     V102 6x   in-burst A   9.429 vs STOCK in-burst   1.233  =>  CONDITIONED ratio   7.65
     V103 6x   in-burst A  15.707 vs STOCK in-burst   1.233  =>  CONDITIONED ratio  12.74
     V104 6x   in-burst A   4.321 vs STOCK in-burst   1.233  =>  CONDITIONED ratio   3.50
     ...against POOLED 21-28 Hz ratios of 57x / 55x / 41x vs stock at this window.
  ⇒ pooling INFLATES the low-speed contrast ~12x, because it compares a 6x arm that is on
    95 %% of the time against a stock arm that is on 5.6 %% of the time.  BOTH numbers are
    real and they answer DIFFERENT questions:
      POOLED     'how different is the car overall'      -> 41-64x  (duty + amplitude)
      CONDITIONED'when it is happening, how much louder' -> 3.5-13x (amplitude only)
    🛑 The duty difference is the larger part of the effect and had never been measured.

